{
  "source": "Prompts/layers-1.mp4",
  "duration": 203.1978125,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.24,
      "text": "Have you ever read a sentence in English class that only made sense after you went back and"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.24,
      "end": 5.04,
      "text": "looked at it a few times?"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.76,
      "end": 6.34,
      "text": "Try this one."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.2,
      "end": 9.12,
      "text": "The horse raced past the barn, fell."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.26,
      "end": 12.54,
      "text": "On a first read, the sentence seems to stop short."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.26,
      "end": 14.2,
      "text": "It feels like a word is missing."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.18,
      "end": 17.7,
      "text": "The horse raced past the barn, and then what?"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.42,
      "end": 22.16,
      "text": "As you reread it, you begin to test each possibility against the words."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.02,
      "end": 27.6,
      "text": "Did the barn fall, or did the horse race past the barn first, and then the horse fell?"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.6,
      "end": 30.56,
      "text": "The correct structure eventually becomes clear."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.28,
      "end": 34.46,
      "text": "Someone raced a horse past a barn, and then that horse fell."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.48,
      "end": 38.1,
      "text": "Each read updates the meaning until the sentence is resolved."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.24,
      "end": 40.34,
      "text": "AI does something similar."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.98,
      "end": 42.66,
      "text": "It builds meaning through repeated updates."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.7,
      "end": 45.04,
      "text": "AI doesn't read like you do."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.6,
      "end": 48.2,
      "text": "It processes text through a specific series of layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.06,
      "end": 53.28,
      "text": "Within each layer, attention and transformation work together to update a set of numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.28,
      "end": 58.38,
      "text": "This process builds sequentially, using the output of one layer as the input for the next."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.16,
      "end": 61.62,
      "text": "The whole stack of layers is called a neural network."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.48,
      "end": 66.92,
      "text": "In this diagram, numbers go in on one side and final numbers come out the other."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.68,
      "end": 70.98,
      "text": "In between, it stands a long line of layers, one after another."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.8,
      "end": 75.24,
      "text": "Each row contains many numbers, though we are only tracking two examples here."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.16,
      "end": 80.76,
      "text": "The starting numbers for these two positions are 0.42 and negative 1.15."
    },
    {
      "start": 81.54,
      "end": 87.02,
      "text": "By the time they reach the end of the sequence, they have shifted to 0.19 and negative 1.12."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.88,
      "end": 90.8,
      "text": "Attention and transformation update the numbers at each layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.5,
      "end": 97.08,
      "text": "As these values shift, the AI is mathematically adjusting how it represents the relationships between your words."
    },
    {
      "start": 98.06,
      "end": 101.24,
      "text": "Let's see this in action by following the word it from layer to layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 101.98,
      "end": 102.72,
      "text": "Here is our sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.86,
      "end": 107.5,
      "text": "The cat sat on the mat during the May rainstorm because it was tired."
    },
    {
      "start": 108.34,
      "end": 112.66,
      "text": "At the start, the pronoun it could refer to the cat, the mat, or the rainstorm."
    },
    {
      "start": 113.4,
      "end": 118.02,
      "text": "The starting numbers 0.12 and negative 0.34 don't tell us which one is the right fit."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.78,
      "end": 123.24,
      "text": "After the first layer, the numbers update to 0.18 and negative 0.22."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.68,
      "end": 127.84,
      "text": "They are beginning to capture a connection between it and cat."
    },
    {
      "start": 128.68,
      "end": 134.66,
      "text": "In the second layer, the numbers update again, carrying more information about that specific connection."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.66,
      "end": 138.1,
      "text": "The process continues through many more layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 138.98,
      "end": 141.2,
      "text": "Each layer builds on the previous layer's numbers,"
    },
    {
      "start": 141.8,
      "end": 144.08,
      "text": "refining the statistical link between the words."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.98,
      "end": 148.7,
      "text": "The values finish at 0.41 and 0.06."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.54,
      "end": 153.62,
      "text": "At this point, the AI works out that it refers to cat."
    },
    {
      "start": 154.48,
      "end": 155.62,
      "text": "Think back to that horse sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 156.34,
      "end": 160.76,
      "text": "It took several reads for your brain to untangle the structure and find the meaning."
    },
    {
      "start": 161.26,
      "end": 163.74,
      "text": "Just as that sentence required extra attention,"
    },
    {
      "start": 164.32,
      "end": 167.38,
      "text": "things like sarcasm or complicated story twists"
    },
    {
      "start": 167.38,
      "end": 171.06,
      "text": "require many more steps to work through the relationships between words."
    },
    {
      "start": 171.98,
      "end": 175.68,
      "text": "This is why AI designs use dozens or even 100 layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 176.52,
      "end": 180.22,
      "text": "Each layer provides another opportunity to refine those complex relationships."
    },
    {
      "start": 181.04,
      "end": 183.9,
      "text": "However, we can't simply add infinite layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 184.66,
      "end": 188.66,
      "text": "Every additional layer requires more computing power and more time to process."
    },
    {
      "start": 189.52,
      "end": 191.46,
      "text": "The extra benefit has to be worth the cost."
    },
    {
      "start": 192.18,
      "end": 194.76,
      "text": "Meaning builds up layer by layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 195.44,
      "end": 199.38,
      "text": "Pause attention and transformation dozens of times."
    }
  ],
